.TH TENSEGRITY 1 "" "Tensegrity" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tensegrity \- train, grow and run byte-level language models
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tensegrity
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tensegrity is a PyTorch toolkit for byte-level language models from 1M to 115M
parameters. It provides data preparation and integrity auditing, resumable
training, generation, evaluation, function-preserving model growth and export.
Models and corpora are provided separately by the user.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Report runtime dependencies and hardware. Add --smoke to run a small training,
checkpoint and generation check, or --json for machine-readable output.
.TP
.B presets
List model sizes and default training budgets.
.TP
.B prepare
Prepare a corpus and write a dataset manifest.
.TP
.B audit
Check the integrity of a prepared dataset.
.TP
.B preflight
Check the model, data and runtime before training.
.TP
.B train
Train or resume a model.
.TP
.B generate
Generate text from a checkpoint.
.TP
.B eval
Evaluate a checkpoint on a dataset.
.TP
.B grow
Grow a trained model into a larger model.
.TP
.B export
Export a checkpoint as safetensors.
.TP
.B report
Write a run report.
.TP
.B probe
Measure context reach and retrieval behavior.
.TP
.B bench
Benchmark generation and attention backends.
.TP
.B continual
Compare continual learning strategies.
.TP
.B convert-checkpoint
Convert a checkpoint into the current format. Legacy pickle loading requires
the explicit --trust-legacy-pickle option and a checkpoint from a trusted source.
.PP
Run
.B tensegrity command --help
for the options supported by each command.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
tensegrity presets
tensegrity --version
tensegrity doctor --smoke
tensegrity prepare --data_path corpus.txt --out_dir data/mine
tensegrity preflight --preset 1m --data_dir data/mine
tensegrity train --preset 1m --data_dir data/mine --out_dir runs/1m --hours 1
tensegrity generate --ckpt runs/1m/ckpt_best.pt --prompt "Hello"
.fi
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/doc/tensegrity-lm/README.md.gz
.RS
Project guide, architecture and research limitations.
.RE
.I /usr/share/doc/tensegrity-lm/README.Debian.gz
.RS
Installation, dependency and package build information.
.RE
.SH NOTES
The Debian package uses the system Python and distribution-provided PyTorch.
CUDA support depends on the installed PyTorch build. Training data and runs are
written only to the paths chosen by the user.
